No.  You assume we are disagreeing on whether reasonable time, place, and
manner restrictions can be imposed.  WE ARE NOT.  NOUS NE SOMMES PAS.  They
can be imposed even in a public forum.  The question of a limited public forum
is one of exclusion.  Can the forum be limited as to participants or
subject matter?  Can a school board allow public hearings but keep the
discussion restricted to school board related matters?  Since keeping the
discussion focused to school board related matters prevents disruption of
school board deliberations, it furthers a significant government interest
(i.e., deliberation).  Because it furthers a significant government interest
and is viewpoint neutral, such a restriction would probably pass
Constitutional scrutiny.  This is something very different from a spam ban.


