Limiting the number of newsgroups that a message can cross-post to is a
limit on the number of possible audiences the message may permissably
reach.  Not everyone subscribes to the same groups.  Although a cross-posted
message may be stored once, to gain visibility, a spammer would want it
linked to a large number of newsgroups so that virtually everyone on Usenet
will see it at least once.


