Netiquette had better not be considered a law.  The documents known
as the netiquette documents are just essays that people with some
net experience wrote to help others understand ways of life on the
net.  I know, I wrote one of the Netiquette documents posted to
news.announce.newusers regularly.

As advisories, and history, they are fine.  Mine is a satire.  But laws?
Hardly.  Laws have to be formulated with the idea of justice, they
are never one person's essay on how things are or should be.

