But look it at another way. The critical resource for a Usenet site
isn't space and it isn't time, it is space*time. A single spam with a
3-day expire might take up 1200 Meg*days, compared to a more typical
post that might take up 3 Meg*days. It seems fairer to me to give
everyone approximately the same Meg*days than to delete 400 peoples'
cheap little messages to clear resources for a spam.

Your (traditional) poster analogy is suggestive. I don't think my lab
would be happy if I removed removed twenty posters so that I could
place my one giant poster on the board. What would make them even more
unhappy would be if I said: the average time a small poster stays up
is a week, I demand that my big poster stay up 1 week, too.

